<p>San Francisco packs a lot of money into roughly seven miles by seven miles. Rent is brutal, but the city is dense, walkable, full of high earners and visited by crowds of tourists and conference-goers every week. That combination means the best side hustles in San Francisco are the ones you can run on foot, by bike or from a laptop, serving people who would rather pay than spend their own time.</p>
<p>Here are 16 side gigs in San Francisco with typical pay, startup costs and the neighborhoods where each works best, plus the city's business registration rules and the California tax details most side hustlers learn the hard way.</p>

