<h2 id="sf-landscape">How San Francisco shapes your side hustle</h2>
<p>A few local realities decide which side jobs in San Francisco are worth your time:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>You do not need a car.</strong> Muni, BART and an e-bike get you almost anywhere, and parking costs can wipe out driving profits. Gigs that work car-free have a real edge.</li>
  <li><strong>The AI boom is real.</strong> Many of the country's best-funded AI startups are clustered in SoMa, Mission Bay and Hayes Valley, and they need contractors, designers, writers and operations help.</li>
  <li><strong>Events and conventions drive surges.</strong> Moscone Center hosts major conferences like Dreamforce, and Outside Lands in Golden Gate Park, Fleet Week, Pride, Bay to Breakers, Giants games at Oracle Park and Warriors and Valkyries games at Chase Center all create spikes in demand.</li>
  <li><strong>Microclimates and hills matter.</strong> The Sunset and Richmond are foggy and residential, the Mission and Dogpatch are sunny and busy. Plan routes around hills and pick a home turf.</li>
</ul>

