<h2 id="by-schedule">Match a side gig to your schedule</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Full-time tech job:</strong> freelancing, deck design, interview-style tutoring and weekend photography fit around a demanding day job without adding a commute.</li>
  <li><strong>Evenings and weekends only:</strong> e-bike delivery, event staffing at Chase Center and Oracle Park, and walking tours on Saturdays and Sundays.</li>
  <li><strong>Daytime gaps:</strong> dog walking, house cleaning and house sitting are busiest while clients are at work.</li>
  <li><strong>Students at SF State, USF or UCSF:</strong> tutoring, convention shifts and delivery by bike pair well with class schedules.</li>
</ul>
<p>Whatever you choose, protect a fixed block of hours every week. In a city this expensive, consistency is what turns a side gig into rent money.</p>

